Z||000000||sdm1964||04-06-2000||08:28 PM||||Can you put the rear exaust manifold without that heat shield on too? It is burned off on one side from leaking for so long. Not the round one but the long flat one that goes between between the manifold and head? has anyone done this? I don't want to create more problems.||||reg||3
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-06-2000||09:32 PM||||Well I have and have not had any problems. This shield is no longer available so what can you do but leave it out. So far in the few Fieros that I have done that to, I've had no problems. I also see a few Fieros come in the shop and they don't have that shield. Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||04-06-2000||09:41 PM||||Have them Jet Hot coated and then you won't need that heat shield.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||04-07-2000||05:18 PM||||I had a new manifold and shield put on my 86 recently.  It came in kit form: Manifold, shield, studs, bolts and some big hose they didn't know what to do with.  I suppose some other gaskets and stuff came in the kit.  I didn't do the work.  It costs about 130.00 from the dealership.  I went through one in Seaside California.  The parts guy, Steve dug it up for me.  Since They had the kit, I figured in not risking going without it, which I almost did.||||reg||4
